ancing-programs/","agency":"IFA / market","color":"5A7488","note":"ESPC moves this off the capital budget. GRID is grant money if the village owns its utility."},{"pct":10,"source":"Capital budget","program":"General fund, bond, or ETCG","url":"https://dceo.illinois.gov/ceja/other-ceja-programs.html","agency":"Village / DCEO","color":"B6C9DA","note":"ETCG covers predevelopment AND capital if the community had a plant or mine closure."}],"crossnote":"CROSS-CHECK against slide 21 of Helpful CEJA Slides. Also on the table for a village, even though it is not in this stack:\n• IEPA Office of Energy — Energy Code training and technical support, wastewater treatment plant energy assessments, Energy Efficiency Trust Fund.\n• IFA Climate Bank — Energy Sovereignty Loan for community ownership, Community Resilience Hubs, Community Charging, C-PACE for private property inside the village, Enabling Upgrades for Solar, Carbon Free Schools.\n• Fleet and transportation — IEPA Electric School Bus and EV Rebate, Charging Incentive Program, and IDOT's NEVI, Carbon Reduction Program, CMAQ and Competitive Freight-Port Infrastructure. Add these the moment the scope touches vehicles.\n• Codes and construction — Building Energy Codes, Stretch Energy Codes, Capital Development Board stretch goals.\n• Housing stock — IHDA Green Resilient Retrofit and Energy Efficiency Program, DCEO Weatherization Assistance.\n• People — Energy Equity Portal, Energy Transition Navigators, Workforce Hubs, Returning Residents, Climate Works.\n• Grid and rates — ICC net metering, Multi-Year Integrated Grid Plans, Equitable Energy Upgrade Program (still in rulemaking).\nNon-energy capital for the same building often sits in a DCEO community development or infrastructure NOFO. Search the full DCEO grant catalog, not just the CEJA page.","first":"First move: check whether the village owns its utility. If it does, GRID and the Small Utility Clean Energy Planning Grant are built only for you."},{"id":"smallbiz","audience":"Small Business Owner","project":"18,000 sf light industrial building — HVAC, envelope, LED, 100 kW rooftop solar","total":"$640,000","facts":["Owner-occupied, taxable entity","Existing banking relationship","Wants payback under 7 years"],"wf":[{"name":"SBDC / Business Information Center","note":"Free help sizing the loan package and the financial statements the lender wants.","agency":"DCEO OEIT"},{"name":"WIOA training dollars via OET","note":"Offsets the cost of retraining staff on the new equipment and controls.","agency":"DCEO OET"},{"name":"Contractor Incubator","note":"If the client is also the installer, this is the bonding and insurance line.","agency":"DCEO"}],"layers":[{"pct":15,"source":"Rebate","program":"Utility custom and prescriptive incentives","url":"https://www.amerenillinoissavings.com/","agency":"ComEd / Ameren / Nicor","color":"0D497F","note":"Apply before you buy equipment. Pre-approval is required on custom measures."},{"pct":12,"source":"Incentive","program":"Illinois Shines — Small DG","url":"https://illinoisshines.com/","agency":"IPA","color":"4A8FC7","note":"Paid through an Approved Vendor. The contractor must hold ICC DG installer certification."},{"pct":25,"source":"Tax credit","program":"Section 48E","url":"https://www.irs.gov/credits-deductions/elective-pay-and-transferability-frequently-asked-questions-overview","agency":"IRS","color":"E0A526","note":"30% base. Must be placed in service by Dec 31, 2027 unless construction started by July 4, 2026."},{"pct":8,"source":"Depreciation","program":"MACRS / bonus depreciation","agency":"IRS","color":"9DBEDA","note":"Real cash value in year one. Your client's CPA, not the installer, sizes this line."},{"pct":30,"source":"Debt","program":"SSBCI Loan Participation or C-PACE","url":"https://illinoisclimatebank.com/financing-programs/developers-contractors/state-small-business-credit-initiative-ssbci/","agency":"IFA Climate Bank","color":"5A7488","note":"SSBCI buys the rate down to 2% max,